{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778979591108,"sessionID":"ses_1cc8dd57fffew3a8dMmS14fA97","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_CRnav6rJaIMGvZulspSLeArL","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/__issue_context__.json","offset":1,"limit":400},"output":"<path>/__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/__issue_context__.json</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: {\n2:   \"body\": \"**Preferred gene-related syndrome label**\\nEFL1-related Shwachman-Diamond syndrome\\n\\n**Synonyms**\\nMONDO:0044205\\n\\n**Parent term (use [OLS](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/mondo), or your favorite ontology browser)**\\n\\n**Definition**\\nAn autosomal recessive syndrome characterized by exocrine pancreatic dysfunction, hematopoietic abnormalities, short stature, and metaphyseal dysplasia and caused by pathogenic variants in the EFL1 gene.\\n\\n\\n**Definition source (Please give PubMed ID, if applicable, in format PMID:#######)\\n\\n**Children terms (if applicable)** Should any existing terms be re-classified as children underneath this new proposed term? \\n\\n**Your nano-attribution (ORCID) or URL for a working group**\\nIf you don't have an ORCID, you can sign up for one [here](https://orcid.org/)\\n\\n\",\n3:   \"comments\": [\n4:     {\n5:       \"id\": \"IC_kwDOBjach87pX9SK\",\n6:       \"author\": {\n7:         \"login\": \"courtneythaxton\"\n8:       },\n9:       \"authorAssociation\": \"MEMBER\",\n10:       \"body\": \"@keparis just checking in if this is a ClinGne expert panel request. If so, please indicate the expert panel that has made this request, thanks!\",\n11:       \"createdAt\": \"2026-02-17T15:26:53Z\",\n12:       \"includesCreatedEdit\": false,\n13:       \"isMinimized\": false,\n14:       \"minimizedReason\": \"\",\n15:       \"reactionGroups\": [],\n16:       \"url\": \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9940#issuecomment-3915371658\",\n17:       \"viewerDidAuthor\": false\n18:     },\n19:     {\n20:       \"id\": \"IC_kwDOBjach87pYNAI\",\n21:       \"author\": {\n22:         \"login\": \"keparis\"\n23:       },\n24:       \"authorAssociation\": \"NONE\",\n25:       \"body\": \"@courtneythaxton Yes, this is for the Childhood, Adolescent, and Young Adult Cancer Predisposition (CAYA) GCEP - thank you!\",\n26:       \"createdAt\": \"2026-02-17T15:38:24Z\",\n27:       \"includesCreatedEdit\": false,\n28:       \"isMinimized\": false,\n29:       \"minimizedReason\": \"\",\n30:       \"reactionGroups\": [],\n31:       \"url\": \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9940#issuecomment-3915436040\",\n32:       \"viewerDidAuthor\": false\n33:     },\n34:     {\n35:       \"id\": \"IC_kwDOBjach88AAAABAya9nA\",\n36:       \"author\": {\n37:         \"login\": \"MeeSiing\"\n38:       },\n39:       \"authorAssociation\": \"MEMBER\",\n40:       \"body\": \"@keparis, thank you for the ticket. The term will be added as exact synonym with ClinGen Preferred label. The update will be available in the upcoming release.\",\n41:       \"createdAt\": \"2026-04-29T21:57:24Z\",\n42:       \"includesCreatedEdit\": false,\n43:       \"isMinimized\": false,\n44:       \"minimizedReason\": \"\",\n45:       \"reactionGroups\": [],\n46:       \"url\": \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9940#issuecomment-4347837852\",\n47:       \"viewerDidAuthor\": false\n48:     }\n49:   ],\n50:   \"title\": \"EFL1-related Shwachman-Diamond syndrome\",\n51:   \"url\": \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9940\"\n52: }\n\n(End of file - total 52 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"{\n  \"body\": \"**Preferred gene-related syndrome label**\\nEFL1-related Shwachman-Diamond syndrome\\n\\n**Synonyms**\\nMONDO:0044205\\n\\n**Parent term (use [OLS](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols/ontologies/mondo), or your favorite ontology browser)**\\n\\n**Definition**\\nAn autosomal recessive syndrome characterized by exocrine pancreatic dysfunction, hematopoietic abnormalities, short stature, and metaphyseal dysplasia and caused by pathogenic variants in the EFL1 gene.\\n\\n\\n**Definition source (Please give PubMed ID, if applicable, in format PMID:#######)\\n\\n**Children terms (if applicable)** Should any existing terms be re-classified as children underneath this new proposed term? \\n\\n**Your nano-attribution (ORCID) or URL for a working group**\\nIf you don't have an ORCID, you can sign up for one [here](https://orcid.org/)\\n\\n\",\n  \"comments\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"IC_kwDOBjach87pX9SK\",\n      \"author\": {\n        \"login\": \"courtneythaxton\"\n      },\n      \"authorAssociation\": \"MEMBER\",\n      \"body\": \"@keparis just checking in if this is a ClinGne expert panel request. If so, please indicate the expert panel that has made this request, thanks!\",\n      \"createdAt\": \"2026-02-17T15:26:53Z\",\n      \"includesCreatedEdit\": false,\n      \"isMinimized\": false,\n      \"minimizedReason\": \"\",\n      \"reactionGroups\": [],\n      \"url\": \"https://github.com/monarch-initiative/mondo/issues/9940#issuecomment-3915371658\",\n      \"viewerDidAuthor\": false\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"IC_kwDOBjach87pYNAI\",","truncated":false,"loaded":[]},"title":"__issue_context__.json","time":{"start":1778979591047,"end":1778979591105}},"id":"prt_e33725378001HH2FBM9mU4gGAu","sessionID":"ses_1cc8dd57fffew3a8dMmS14fA97","messageID":"msg_e33724793001Sj9ReDgfiR4s7A"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1778979591121,"sessionID":"ses_1cc8dd57fffew3a8dMmS14fA97","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"skill","callID":"call_uBNwmcTGUP52oj2I3NjhXHlh","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"name":"task-coordinator"},"output":"<skill_content name=\"task-coordinator\">\n# Skill: task-coordinator\n\nYou are the MONDO Ontology Task Coordinator, a master planner responsible for orchestrating all ontology work in the MONDO project. You MUST be used first for ANY ontology task to ensure proper planning, execution, and validation.\n\nYour core responsibilities:\n\n1. **Task Analysis & Decomposition**: Break down complex ontology requests into logical, sequential steps. Consider all aspects: research needs, design patterns, validation requirements, and potential risks.\n\n2. **Agent Orchestration**: Plan the optimal sequence of specialized agents:\n   - Start with deep-research-specialist for literature review when PMIDs are mentioned\n   - Use design-pattern-advisor to ensure compliance with MONDO patterns\n   - Coordinate execution agents for the actual ontology work\n   - Always include identifier-validator to prevent hallucinated IDs\n   - End with obo-checkin for term integration\n   - Use ontology-reasoner when logical definitions are involved\n\n3. **Critical Validation Oversight**: You are the final safeguard against:\n   - Hallucinated MONDO IDs, PMIDs, or gene identifiers\n   - Missing required metadata (definitions, sources, proper citations)\n   - Violations of MONDO naming conventions\n   - Incomplete check-in processes\n\n4. **Quality Assurance Protocol**: Ensure every task includes:\n   - Proper literature research when references are provided\n   - Design pattern compliance checking\n   - Identifier validation (especially for genes using HGNC or NCBI gene)\n   - Complete source attribution\n   - Syntax validation before check-in\n   - Reasoner validation for logical definitions\n\n5. **Risk Management**: Flag high-risk scenarios:\n   - New term creation without proper research\n   - Obsolescence without replacement planning\n   - Missing or incorrect gene identifiers\n   - Inadequate source citations\n\nYour planning output should specify:\n- The exact sequence of agents to use\n- Key validation checkpoints\n- Specific risks to monitor\n- Required deliverables at each step\n\nNEVER allow any ontology work to proceed without proper planning, validation, and check-in procedures. You are responsible for maintaining the integrity and quality of the MONDO ontology through systematic coordination of all specialized agents.\n\nBase directory for this skill: file:///__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/.claude/skills/task-coordinator\nRelative paths in this skill (e.g., scripts/, reference/) are relative to this base directory.\nNote: file list is sampled.\n\n<skill_files>\n\n</skill_files>\n</skill_content>","metadata":{"name":"task-coordinator","dir":"/__w/eval-ont-agent-mondo/eval-ont-agent-mondo/.claude/skills/task-coordinator","truncated":false},"title":"Loaded skill: task-coordinator","time":{"start":1778979591073,"end":1778979591119}},"id":"prt_e3372539c001frgHohuWishxCx","sessionID":"ses_1cc8dd57fffew3a8dMmS14fA97","messageID":"msg_e33724793001Sj9ReDgfiR4s7A"}}
